{"t":1794297287577,"event":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011CgttRo6p1guzrmjzsCiiH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Implementation Paused\n\n**Change:** add-room-bookings\n**Schema:** spec-driven\n**Progress:** 30/34 tasks complete\n\nThe code for all of groups 1–7 is written and `pnpm run build`, `pnpm run lint` and `pnpm run test` all exit 0. The four live-stack checks (8.2–8.5) are not done, because `curl` is still not permitted in this session and there is no browser tool for 8.5.\n\n### What is verified\n- **Build, lint, test:** all three succeed for the 7 projects, and nothing changed under `libs/contract`, `apps/room` or `apps/web/src/views/rooms`.\n- **Migration (1.3):** `migration:run`, then `migration:revert`, then `migration:run` all succeeded against the local database.\n- **Startup:** with the stack up, `booking`, `worker` and `gateway` started cleanly, the five `/api/bookings` routes were mapped, and no log held an error line.\n\n### What is not verified\n- **8.2–8.4:** no booking has been created against real Postgres, Redis and NATS. The idempotent create, the ten-parallel-requests guarantee and the confirmation outcomes rest on mocked unit tests only.\n- **8.5:** the `/bookings` page has not been opened against the gateway.\n\nThe stack is stopped. The check script for 8.2–8.4 is ready at `tmp/checks/api.sh` (git-ignored); it expects the gateway on port 3110.\n\n### One fix I made after the agents finished\nThe two new entities imported `@roombook/contract` at runtime, which the migration CLI cannot resolve, so `migration:run` failed on the first stack start. They now use type-only imports, and the column default is the literal `'PENDING'`.\n\n### Deviations to review\n- **Boolean replies:** the `DELETE` and `RECORD_CONFIRMATION` handlers in the booking service reply a boolean, because the backend agent found that a reply without a value makes the NATS caller fail. The gateway still answers 204 with an empty body.\n- **Jest config:** `setupFiles: ['reflect-metadata']` was added to `jest.config.ts` in `apps/booking`, `apps/gateway` and `apps/worker`; specs that import the contract first fail without it.\n- **Delete error location:** the delete dialog only confirms or declines; the API message appears in an alert on the page, as D9 says. Task 7.5 can be read as wanting it in the dialog.\n- **Files beyond the design:**\n  - a backend test fixture, `apps/booking/src/booking/testing/booking.fixture.ts`;\n  - a web test fixture, `booking-test-data.ts`;\n  - two split spec files, `booking.service.create.spec.ts` and `bookings-page-actions.spec.tsx`, to stay under 200 lines.\n- **Unspecified page behaviour:** deleting the last row on a later page steps back one page; the page size is fixed at 10.\n- **`updatedAt`:** the backend agent expects it to move on an empty PATCH and when a confirmation outcome is recorded; the spec does not say either way.\n\n### Known risk, not changed\nTwo concurrent first requests whose idempotency keys differ only in letter case would both pass the advisory lock; the primary key rejects the second, so it would get a 500 rather than a duplicate booking. Lower-casing the key in the service would close it, but that is outside the specs.\n\n### Options\n1. Allow `curl` and `bash tmp/checks/api.sh` for this project (for example in `.claude/settings.json`) and rerun `/opsx:apply`; I then start the stack and finish 8.2–8.4.\n2. Run it yourself: `pnpm run stack:up`, then `bash tmp/checks/api.sh`, and send me the output to check against the specs.\n3. For 8.5, open `/bookings` on the web port that `stack:up` prints and walk the page by hand, or give me a browser tool."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":796,"cache_read_input_tokens":150615,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":796},"output_tokens":755,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c68e55db-2b10-4383-aa2a-5106ff8e45ae","uuid":"87228ce8-2f9a-4924-b655-a6e5dc3f052f","timestamp":"2026-11-10T07:54:47.573Z","request_id":"req_011CgttRnrvti6xLgwvS5mGY"}}
